    summary: "Speech verbs such as hissed, growled, breathed, purred, exclaimed and opined make a tag do the work of the line, and some, such as smiled or laughed, are not speech at all. Many editors favour said and asked, which readers skim past, but a well-chosen verb is a legitimate tool.",
