    name: "Stock gestures: nodded, shrugged, sighed, smiled",
    summary: "Characters in drafts nod, shrug, sigh, smile, frown and look away so often that the gestures stop meaning anything. They are the handy stage directions of prose, and readers learn to skip them; specific, character-bound business reads fresher and tells more.",
