    name: "Throat-clearing and padding phrases",
    summary: "Phrases such as it should be noted that, the fact that, in order to, due to the fact that and at this point in time add words without adding meaning. They are common in speech and official writing, and trimming them is a standard way to tighten prose, though a few set a rhythm or tone.",
