    name: "Echo words and unintended repetition",
    summary: "Echo words are repeats of the same word or sound within a few lines, such as two uses of turned in one paragraph or three sentences ending in -ing. Readers hear them even when they cannot name them, and a read-aloud or a word search finds them; repetition is a tool only when it is chosen.",
